# Project context

**At the start of a session and before non-trivial work, read [`.cursor/context.md`](../context.md).**
It is the Cursor boot map: product shape, layering, hard rules, and where to put new code.

Canonical rules (do not duplicate elsewhere) live in `.ai/`, shared with Codex and Claude
Code through `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`. After the context file, read as needed:

- `.ai/project.md` — what the service is and where its boundaries are
- `.ai/structure.md` — the repository map, layering, where new code belongs
- `.ai/conventions.md` — the rules of this codebase (read before writing code)
- `.ai/journal.md` — the last few entries, for the current state

Architecture in depth: `docs/overview.md`. Core pipeline DAG: `docs/core-pipeline.md`.

# Log the change

When a task is finished, append an entry to `.ai/journal.md` before reporting back, using
the template at the top of that file. Record the decision and what was rejected, not the
keystrokes — a diff already shows which lines moved.

Write down anything about the codebase that cost you time: a hanging test package, stale
generated code, a surprising invariant. That is the part the next assistant cannot recover
from the diff.

# Language

Go code and tests are commented in Russian. The API contract and everything under
`internal/ui/web/static` are English, comments included — three tests enforce that split.
Comments explain why, never what, and never the change you just made.
